{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0016_macron_index_variants_are_own_entries_and_index_is_repaired_not_regenerated", "label": "ADR 0016: Macron-index variants are own entries; index is repaired not regenerated", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0016-macron-index-variants-are-own-entries-and-index-is-repaired-not-regenerated.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "status": "accepted", "amends": "0015", "rationale": "Mapping every variant to the entry's first bold headword produced wrong index forms such as \u00e6r\u00feling to \u01e3rst. The packaged index is curated data (ambiguous_completed, ambiguous_metadata, and diacritic add / diacritic-disambiguate additions), so regenerating it from oe_bt.txt would destroy that curation and drop marks. A variant is indexed only with the spelling its heading gives it, and repair prunes or adds keys without replacing the file."}, {"id": "packaged_macron_index", "label": "Packaged macron index oe_bt_macron_index.json", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "docs/adr/0016-macron-index-variants-are-own-entries-and-index-is-repaired-not-regenerated.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "wyrdcraeft/etc/diacritic/oe_bt_macron_index.json is curated data, not a build artifact. It holds disambiguation state and manual additions. bin/build_macron_index.py output is merge input, not a replacement. Repair pruned entries whose display form does not normalize to their key and added missing variants without overwriting existing keys."}, {"id": "macron_index_alternate_checkout", "label": "Differently cleaned macron-index source checkout", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0016-macron-index-variants-are-own-entries-and-index-is-repaired-not-regenerated.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": 